Package: ssNRI
Type: Package
Title: Sample Size Calculation for Trials with Non-Responder Imputation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given  = "Gosuke",
    family = "Homma",
    role   = c("aut", "cre"),
    email  = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com"
  )
Description: Sample size and operating characteristics for two-group superiority
    trials with a binary endpoint in which dropouts are handled by non-responder
    imputation (NRI). Latent response and dropout indicators are modelled jointly
    as a bivariate Bernoulli distribution, so that the association between
    response and dropout, the group-specific dropout probabilities, and the
    allocation ratio can all be specified directly. Provides closed-form sample
    size formulas for the dropout-free design, for a complete case analysis under
    the simple inflation method, and for NRI, together with exact power and exact
    type I error rate obtained by complete enumeration of the joint outcome
    distribution.
